course: dictionary
lesson: 6933
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is meant. The word paddy is a good example. «In Belfast, Uncle Paddy pulls a coin from Ronan's ear at every single party.» Paddy has a capital letter and does a magic trick, so it is a person's name.
explain: «Rice grows in flooded fields called paddies in warm countries.» Here a paddy is a field, because the words flooded fields and rice show you where it is. The clues around the word lead you to the right meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If paddy means a fit of bad temper, does «He's in a paddy» make sense? It does, and that is the clue that this meaning is used in everyday talk in the UK.
fact: A paddy is a flooded field where rice is grown.
fact: Paddy can also mean rice that has not yet been husked.
fact: In UK informal speech, a paddy is a fit of bad temper, as in «He's in a paddy».
fact: Paddy is also a short form of the name Patrick.
fact: «Paddy» is an old insulting word for an Irish person, so never use it.
exercise: «Rice grows in flooded fields called paddies.» What is a paddy here? | A fit of bad temper | A short form of a name | A kind of bird | *A flooded field where rice is grown
exercise: «He's in a paddy because his game got cancelled.» What does paddy mean? | A friendly dog | *A fit of bad temper | A flooded field | Rice that has not been husked
exercise: In «Uncle Paddy pulls a coin from Ronan's ear», what kind of word is Paddy? | *A name | A type of rice | A field | A kind of insect
test: «Some farmers keep ducks in the paddy to eat pests and weeds.» What does paddy mean? | A name | Husked rice | A fit of temper | *A flooded rice field
test: «Ronan is 10 now and still laughs at Paddy's trick.» Is Paddy a name here? | No, it is a type of rice | No, it means a temper | *Yes, a person's name | No, it is always a field
exam: Which sentence uses paddy to mean a fit of bad temper? | Rice can grow in flooded fields because air passes down spongy tubes | Rice is grown in warm countries and more than half of all people eat it | *«She threw a paddy when the bus was late.» | «Uncle Paddy pulls a coin from Ronan's ear at every party.»
